            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "crazyblonde"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This rub was fantastic...I used it on skinless thighs..Only thing different I did was after marinating all nite, I poured some olive oil on top and worked it into the rub...refrigerated again till that evening...The meat was so moist and tender with a great flavor...cant wait to try on my ribs..."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Toasty Mama"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yummy! Halved the recipe, mixed with some olive oil and rubbed it over/under the skin and in the cavity of a roasting chicken. SO GOOD! Baked in a roaster in my oven for two hours and basted with Famous Amos's BBQ once five minutes before it was done. Chicken stayed moist and it was so full of flavor. Can't wait to try it on ribs!",
            "datePublished": "2009-03-20T17:33:49.997Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SLJ6"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Cut this recipe in half and omitted the white pepper since I had none. I used this on a 3-4lb beef rump roast that I let marinate overnight in the fridge in this rub. Yesterday morning I put it in the crockpot for 8-9 hours on low and then shredded for sandwiches. I used Smokin' Jack's BBQ Sauce from this site to top these amazing sandwiches. Excellent!!!",
            "datePublished": "2012-08-26T08:53:16.493Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Nikki"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Instead of crushed red pepper I used cayenne and added ground corriander and cumin. Left out the salt and ground pepper in the spices and just added it directly to the meat. I've used this recipe in backyard competitions.",
            "datePublished": "2019-04-23T20:45:59.760Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "New2This"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I loved this recipe. I used it on Pork Tenderloin and grilled it on the BBQ for about an hour, turning every 10-15 minutes. I put less pepper in and it still had quite a bit of kick to it! I made it for my in-laws and they loved it too! I had some left over, so I will try it on chicken next. Thanks for the great recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2009-09-26T09:26:02.893Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Cat Berner"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a great rub, we used it on pork chops. I left out the white pepper, and I'm glad I did, otherwise it would have gotten too spicy. This rub will become a staple in our house.",
            "datePublished": "2007-07-21T13:53:47.743Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kali Doogarsingh"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I had to give this rub its props....after all, it got rave reviews from my family. I rubbed it on some babyback ribs and baked them in the oven for 2 hours. My brother said they were better than restaurant ribs!!!",
            "datePublished": "2007-09-14T16:53:30.127Z"
          },
